.TH PO-TRANSLATE 1 "February 2026" "po-translate 1.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
po-translate \- batch translate PO and TS localization files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B po-translate
\fB\-\-source\fR \fILANG\fR [\fB\-\-target\fR \fILANG\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPATH\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B po-translate
automatically translates GNU gettext .po and Qt Linguist .ts files using
various translation services, including free services, commercial APIs,
and AI-powered translation models. It preserves file structure, metadata,
and formatting while translating only untranslated entries.

The tool supports both batch processing of multiple files and directories,
as well as single-file operations. It can work with translation glossaries
for consistent terminology and provides dry-run capabilities for previewing
changes before applying them.

If \fB\-\-target\fR is not specified, the target language is automatically
detected from the \fBLANG\fR environment variable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display comprehensive help message with all available options and usage
examples, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version number, build information, and supported features, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-s " " \fILANG\fR ", " \-\-source " " \fILANG\fR
Source language code (required). Must be a valid ISO 639-1 or RFC 5646
language code. Examples: 'en', 'en-US', 'pt-BR'. This language should
match the original text in the localization files.
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fILANG\fR ", " \-\-target " " \fILANG\fR
Target language code for translation output. Uses the same format as
source language. If not specified, defaults to the language extracted
from the system \fBLANG\fR environment variable.
.TP
.BR \-\-service " " \fISERVICE\fR
Translation service to use (default: lingva). Each service has different
characteristics in terms of quality, speed, cost, and API requirements.
See SERVICES section for detailed information about each provider.
.TP
.BR \-\-api\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
API key for commercial and AI-powered services. Required for deepl,
deepl-free, google, openai, and anthropic services. Can also be provided
via environment variables (see ENVIRONMENT section).
.TP
.BR \-\-url " " \fIURL\fR
Custom server URL for LibreTranslate or other compatible self-hosted
translation services. Useful for private LibreTranslate instances or
alternative endpoints. Must be a complete URL including protocol.
.TP
.BR \-\-model " " \fIMODEL\fR
Specific model to use for AI translation services. Only applicable to
openai and anthropic services. Examples: 'gpt-4o-mini', 'gpt-4o',
'claude-3-haiku-20240307', 'claude-3-sonnet-20240229'. Different
models offer trade-offs between speed, quality, and cost.
.TP
.BR \-\-batch\-size " " \fIN\fR
Number of translation entries to process in a single API call (default: 10).
Larger batch sizes can improve efficiency but may hit API limits or
cause timeouts. Smaller batches provide more granular progress feedback
and error recovery.
.TP
.BR \-\-glossary " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to a glossary file for consistent translation of terminology.
Supports multiple formats: CSV (source,target), TSV (tab-separated),
and TBX (TermBase eXchange). Glossary terms take precedence over
service translations for matching strings.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Preview mode that processes files and shows what translations would be
applied without actually modifying any files. Useful for testing
service configurations and reviewing potential changes before commitment.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-recursive
Disable recursive directory searching. When specified, only process
files directly in the given directories without descending into
subdirectories. Useful for controlled processing of large directory
structures.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Format all output as JSON for programmatic consumption and integration
with automation scripts. Progress updates, results, and statistics
are provided in structured JSON format. Error messages remain in
plain text to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output including progress indicators and
informational messages. Only display errors and the final summary.
Exit codes still indicate success/failure status.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-verbose
Enable detailed progress output including API call details, timing
information, batch processing status, individual entry results, and
service-specific diagnostic information. Useful for debugging and
performance analysis.
.TP
.BR \-\-about
Display comprehensive application information including version details,
supported file formats, available services, feature overview, and
licensing information, then exit.
.SH SERVICES
.B po-translate
supports multiple translation services with different characteristics:

.TP
.B lingva (default)
Free translation service using Lingva Translate instances. No API key
required. Supports many language pairs with reasonable quality. May
have rate limiting during peak usage. Best for: casual use, testing,
non-commercial projects.

.TP
.B mymemory
Translated.net's MyMemory service. Offers a free tier with 1000 words
per day without registration. Higher limits available with API keys.
Combines machine translation with translation memory. Best for: small
projects, occasional use.

.TP
.B libretranslate
Open-source neural machine translation. Can use public instances or
self-hosted deployments via \-\-url. Good balance of quality and privacy.
No API key required for public instances. Best for: privacy-conscious
users, self-hosted environments.

.TP
.B deepl
Premium neural machine translation service known for high-quality
results, especially for European languages. Requires API key and paid
subscription. Offers excellent handling of context and idioms.
Best for: professional translations, high-quality requirements.

.TP
.B deepl-free
Free tier of DeepL service with monthly usage limits. Requires free
API key registration. Same quality as paid DeepL but with restrictions
on volume and features. Best for: evaluation, low-volume professional use.

.TP
.B google
Google Cloud Translation API. Requires Google Cloud account and API key.
Supports extensive language pairs with neural machine translation.
Integration with Google's language detection and other services.
Best for: enterprise integration, Google Cloud environments.

.TP
.B openai
AI-powered translation using OpenAI's GPT models. Requires API key.
Provides context-aware translations with understanding of nuance
and cultural adaptation. Can handle complex technical terminology
and maintain consistent tone. Best for: high-quality creative content,
technical documentation.

.TP
.B anthropic
Claude AI models for translation. Requires API key. Offers careful
attention to context, cultural sensitivity, and maintaining original
meaning. Excellent for nuanced content and complex linguistic
requirements. Best for: literary content, cultural adaptation,
complex technical material.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All translations completed successfully without errors or warnings.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error occurred such as invalid API credentials, network failures,
unsupported language pairs, or file access problems.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Translate files to system language (auto-detected from LANG):
.B po-translate \-\-source en messages.po
.TP
Batch translate directory from English to Swedish:
.B po-translate \-\-source en \-\-target sv locale/
.TP
Use DeepL with API key for high-quality translation:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t de \-\-service deepl \-\-api\-key $DEEPL_API_KEY file.po
.TP
Preview OpenAI translation without saving:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t fr \-\-service openai \-\-dry\-run translations/
.TP
Use custom LibreTranslate instance:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t es \-\-service libretranslate \-\-url https://translate.example.com
.TP
Translate with glossary for consistent terminology:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t ja \-\-glossary terms.csv locale/
.TP
Use AI with specific model and larger batches:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t de \-\-service openai \-\-model gpt\-4o \-\-batch\-size 5 src.po
.TP
Quiet processing with JSON output for automation:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t ru \-\-quiet \-\-json \-\-service mymemory po/
.TP
Verbose translation with timing information:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t zh \-\-verbose \-\-service deepl\-free docs/
.TP
Non-recursive processing of specific directory:
.B po-translate \-s en \-t ko \-\-no\-recursive \-\-service google top\-level/
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANG
Default target language when \-\-target is not specified. The language
code is extracted from the locale format (e.g., 'sv_SE.UTF-8' becomes 'sv').
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
API key for OpenAI service. Used automatically when \-\-service is openai
and no \-\-api\-key is provided.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
API key for Anthropic service. Used automatically when \-\-service is
anthropic and no \-\-api\-key is provided.
.TP
.B DEEPL_API_KEY
API key for DeepL services. Used automatically when \-\-service is
deepl or deepl\-free and no \-\-api\-key is provided.
.TP
.B GOOGLE_API_KEY
API key for Google Cloud Translation. Used automatically when
\-\-service is google and no \-\-api\-key is provided.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B *.po
GNU gettext Portable Object files (primary format)
.TP
.B *.ts
Qt Linguist Translation Source files
.TP
.B *.pot
GNU gettext Portable Object Template files (read-only)
.TP
.B ~/.config/po-translate/
User configuration directory
.TP
.B ~/.config/po-translate/glossaries/
Default location for glossary files
